// fix-health-app-v2.4.11.cjs — Family Health Track v2.4.11 one-step fix
// Run from the project root (the folder with package.json) with:
//   node fix-health-app-v2.4.11.cjs
// Requires v2.4.10 already applied (run fix-health-app-v2.4.10.cjs first if you
// are still on v2.4.9). What it does:
//   1. Backs up each changed file to <file>.bak (first run only)
//   2. Applies the v2.4.11 fix — ALL remaining audit issues: record saves
//      that failed silently now show an error; dates use Myanmar local
//      time; fake prefilled values removed; in-app password reset in
//      Burmese; first-run welcome guide; no more "healthy" with zero data;
//      phone-only data is now per-user (shared phone is private again);
//      admin can answer/add records from the patient detail view; CSV
//      export covers all types and import is batched; twice-daily meds;
//      child fever in Celsius; Health News relabelled as a knowledge
//      library; Emergency ID gains DOB / contact relation / conditions
//   3. Runs npm install, typecheck (tsc), tests (vitest) and build
// Safe to run twice: files already matching the new content are skipped.
// It does NOT touch your data, your Firebase project, or git.
// NOTE: this version does NOT change firestore.rules — no Console step
// is needed for the rules. (The v2.4.10 rules still need to be published
// if you have not published them yet.)
